# matmul_bfp8_b_swiglu.cbtable
#   The FUSED-SWIGLU resident matmul (program rtriad_bfp8_swiglu, -DFT_RTRIAD_SWIGLU=1):
#   matmul_bfp8_b.cbtable's three CBs, unchanged, plus the two the SILU_MUL half needs
#   (kernels/resident_matmul_swiglu_protocol.h) and the one the S3a residual add needs
#   (-DFT_RTRIAD_RESADD=1, kernels/resident_matmul_resadd_protocol.h):
#
#     cb  0  Float16_b  2048 B   activations
#     cb  1  Bfp8_b     1088 B   weights
#     cb  2  Float16_b  2048 B   stage: silu(gate) packed bf16 (eltwise_float16b's cb 2)
#     cb  3  Float16_b  2048 B   panel: a column block's gate tiles, then its up tiles
#                                (S3a: the block's bf16(A . B) tiles, then pad)
#     cb  4  Float16_b  2048 B   residual: a column block's residual tiles (eltwise ADD's cb 0)
#     cb 16  Float16_b  2048 B   output
#
#   math_fidelity, approx and dst_accum_mode are matmul_bfp8_b's AND eltwise_float16b's
#   (HiFi4, exact, fp32 DST), so the matmul half is the shipped matmul and the SILU_MUL (ADD)
#   half is the shipped eltwise SILU_MUL (ADD), rounding point for rounding point. cb 0's
#   Float16_b keeps
#   the intermediate format Float16_b, so the emitted cb 0/1/16 arrays are matmul_bfp8_b's.

math_fidelity  4
approx         0
dst_accum_mode 1

cb  0  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb  1  Bfp8_b    32 32 16 4
cb  2  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb  3  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb  4  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb 16  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
